<html>
  <head>
    <style>
      body{
        font-family: -apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,"Segoe UI",Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif,"Apple Color Emoji","Segoe UI Emoji";
      }
      @media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
        html { background: #000D; color: #EEE; }
        a { color: #669df5; }
        a:visited { color: #af73d5; }
      }
    </style>
  </head>

  <body>
    <div style="text-align: center; margin: 60px 120px 0px">
      <img alt="Mona looking at a book of code and dancing" src="<%= image_path "mona-code.gif" %>">
      <h1>
        Looking for Lookbook?
      </h1>
      <p>
        It seems you have the <code>SKIP_LOOKBOOK</code> environment variable set, which is preventing Lookbook from being mounted.
      </p>
      <p>
        Restart your server with <code>env -u SKIP_LOOKBOOK script/server</code> to clear the environment variable
        (or run <code>unset SKIP_LOOKBOOK</code> to clear it for the rest of the session).
        Lookbook will then be available at this URL.
      </p>
      <p>
        You can also view components at <a class="Link--inTextBlock" href="http://github.localhost/rails/view_components/">http://github.localhost/rails/view_components/</a>, even when Lookbook is skipped.
      </p>
      <p>
        For more about exactly which environment variables affect Lookbook, see <code>config/routes.rb</code>.
      </p>
      <p>
        <i><a class="Link--inTextBlock" href="https://thehub.github.com/epd/engineering/dev-practicals/frontend/development-environments/#lookbook-in-development">
          Read more about Lookbook on The Hub.
        </a></i>
      </p>
    </div>
  </body>
</html>
